{"content":[{"c":["FORGETFULNESS, Land of"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Euphemism for the abode of the dead. Once in the land of forgetfulness, the dead are thought to be forgotten by God (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.88.12","r":"Ps.88.12","rawR":"Ps.88.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.88.12","value":"Ps.88.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 88:12"},") and people (",{"href":"?bref=Eccl.9.5-6","r":"Eccl.9.5-6","rawR":"Eccl.9.5-6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Eccl.9.5-6","value":"Eccl.9.5-6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Eccl 9:5-6"},") alike. ",{"href":"?bref=Job.14.21-22","r":"Job.14.21-22","rawR":"Job.14.21-22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.14.21-22","value":"Job.14.21-22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Job 14:21-22"},", suggests, however, that the deceased retain some self-consciousness in Sheol."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Sheol_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Sheol_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Sheol_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Sheol"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"ForgetfulnessLandof","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Ps 88:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.88.12","rawQueryValue":"Ps.88.12","sourceRefExact":"Ps.88.12"},{"anchorText":"Eccl 9:5-6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Eccl.9.5-6","rawQueryValue":"Eccl.9.5-6","sourceRefExact":"Eccl.9.5-6"},{"anchorText":"Job 14:21-22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Job.14.21-22","rawQueryValue":"Job.14.21-22","sourceRefExact":"Job.14.21-22"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"d2219e3199eff3a8303149ce20bb6142db8a981f40d70fd96747d4e440bf460c","sourceItemName":"ForgetfulnessLandof","sourceItemOrder":67,"sourceMember":"Articles/F.xml","suppleme